    "created_at": "2016-04-15T17:12:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-15T17:12:14Z",
    "body": "(I am against semantic line breaking, and prefer breaking inside tags. Keep the rules simple: break at 100, break at any space. The current rules are good.)\n\nThis seems like a hard problem to solve unless we want to do a one-time giant reformat. There are large sections (e.g. bibliography, acknowledgments, terms defined in other specs) which do not follow the 100 character rule, on purpose. For acknowledgments especially it would be disastrous.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
